    <para styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">The &quot;Edit</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-style:italic; color:#800000;" translate="true"> </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">Unit</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-style:italic; color:#800000;" translate="true"> </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">Search</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-style:italic; color:#800000;" translate="true"> </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">Path&quot; expert helps you edit the unit search path of the current project. It provides easy access to the unit search paths of all targets configured for it. A configurable favorites menu gives access to frequently used paths.</text></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:center; margin-top:40px; margin-right:6px; margin-bottom:40px; margin-left:6px;"><image src="EditUnitSearchPath10Main.png" imagestyleclass="Default" scale="100.00%" styleclass="Image Caption" figurelistinclude="0"></image></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px;"><table styleclass="Default" rowcount="2" colcount="2" style="width:100%; background-color:#f4f4f4;">
      <tr style="vertical-align:top">
        <td style="width:48px;">
          <para styleclass="Normal" style="margin-top:3px; margin-bottom:3px; margin-left:6px;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; color:#ff0000;" translate="true">Notice</text></para>
        </td>
        <td style="vertical-align:top;">
          <list id="0" type="ul" listtype="bullet" formatstring="&#167;" format-charset="SYMBOL_CHARSET" levelreset="true" legalstyle="false" startfrom="1" styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:3px; margin-right:6px; margin-bottom:3px; margin-left:8px; font-family:Wingdings; font-size:10pt; color:#000000;">
            <li styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:3px; margin-right:6px; margin-bottom:3px; margin-left:8px;"><text styleclass=" " style="font-family:Verdana; font-size:10pt; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; text-decoration:none; text-transform:none; vertical-align:baseline; color:#000000; background-color:transparent; letter-spacing:normal; letter-scaling:100%;" translate="true">This expert is only available in </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">Delphi versions from Delphi</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-style:italic; color:#800000;" translate="true"> </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">2009 and later because the OTAPI did not offer access to the target list in earlier versions. </text></li>
          </list>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr style="vertical-align:top">
        <td style="width:48px;">
          <para styleclass="Normal" style="margin-top:3px; margin-bottom:3px; margin-left:6px;"><text styleclass=" " style="font-family:Verdana; font-size:10pt; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; text-decoration:none; text-transform:none; vertical-align:baseline; color:#000000; background-color:transparent; letter-spacing:normal; letter-scaling:100%;" translate="true">&#32;</text></para>
        </td>
        <td style="vertical-align:top;">
          <list id="1" type="ul" listtype="bullet" formatstring="&#167;" format-charset="SYMBOL_CHARSET" levelreset="true" legalstyle="false" startfrom="1" styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:3px; margin-right:6px; margin-bottom:3px; margin-left:8px; font-family:Wingdings; font-size:10pt; color:#000000;">
            <li styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:3px; margin-right:6px; margin-bottom:3px; margin-left:8px;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">In </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; text-decoration:underline;" translate="true">all</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true"> Delphi versions from Delphi</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-style:italic; color:#800000;" translate="true"> </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">6 and later t</text><text styleclass=" " style="font-family:Verdana; font-size:10pt; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; text-decoration:none; text-transform:none; vertical-align:baseline; color:#000000; background-color:transparent; letter-spacing:normal; letter-scaling:100%;" translate="true">he &quot;</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">IDE Enhancement for search paths&quot; should work - the functionality of the enhancement is similar to the capabilities of this expert, albeit more restricted. </text></li>
          </list>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><anchor id="Details" styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-weight:bold;"></anchor><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-size:16pt;" translate="true"> &#160; </text></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><table styleclass="Default" rowcount="1" colcount="2" style="width:100%; cell-padding:0px; cell-spacing:0px; background-color:#cfe7ff;">
      <tr style="vertical-align:middle">
        <td style="height:24px; background-color:#cfe7ff;">
          <para styleclass="Normal" style="margin-left:6px; page-break-inside:avoid; page-break-after:avoid;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Details </text></para>
        </td>
        <td style="width:40px; height:24px; background-color:#cfe7ff;">
          <para styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:right; margin-top:3px; margin-right:6px;"><link displaytype="image" src="__Jump2Top.png" type="topiclink" href=""><title translate="true">Jump to top of page</title></link></para>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px; border:none;"><anchor id="Target" styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;"></anchor><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-size:16pt;" translate="true"> &#160; </text></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px;"><table styleclass="Default" rowcount="1" colcount="2" style="width:100%; border-width:0px; border-spacing:0px; border-collapse:collapse; cell-border-width:1px; border-color:#000000; border-style:solid;">
      <tr style="vertical-align:top">
        <td style="border-top:none; border-right:none; border-left:none;">
          <para styleclass="Normal" style="page-break-after:avoid;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Target </text></para>
        </td>
        <td style="vertical-align:top; width:20px; border-top:none; border-right:none; border-left:none;">
          <para styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:right;"><link displaytype="image" src="__Jump2Top.png" type="topiclink" href=""><title translate="true">Jump to top of page</title></link></para>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table></para>
    <list id="2" type="ul" listtype="bullet" formatstring="&#167;" format-charset="SYMBOL_CHARSET" levelreset="true" legalstyle="false" startfrom="1" styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px; font-family:Wingdings; font-size:10pt; color:#000000;">
      <li styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">The target list shows all compiler targets configured for the current project. </text></li>
      <li styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">By default, the currently active compiler target of the project is preselected. This behavior can be changed in the configuration; the configuration dialog is accessible from in the GExperts configuration dialog. </text></li>
      <li styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">You can select the desired target with the </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-style:italic; color:#800000;" translate="true">mouse</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true"> or with </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-style:italic; color:#800000;" translate="true">Alt + up/down arrow keys</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">. </text></li>
    </list>
    <list id="3" type="ul" listtype="bullet" formatstring="&#167;" format-charset="SYMBOL_CHARSET" levelreset="true" legalstyle="false" startfrom="1" styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px; font-family:Wingdings; font-size:10pt; color:#000000;">
      <li styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">The list does not provide options for creating or deleting targets; this must be done in the IDE. </text></li>
    </list>
    <para styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px; border:none;"><anchor id="UnitSearchPath" styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;"></anchor><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-size:16pt;" translate="true"> &#160; </text></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px;"><table styleclass="Default" rowcount="1" colcount="2" style="width:100%; border-width:0px; border-spacing:0px; border-collapse:collapse; cell-border-width:1px; border-color:#000000; border-style:solid;">
      <tr style="vertical-align:top">
        <td style="border-top:none; border-right:none; border-left:none;">
          <para styleclass="Normal" style="page-break-after:avoid;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Unit Search Path </text></para>
        </td>
        <td style="vertical-align:top; width:20px; border-top:none; border-right:none; border-left:none;">
          <para styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:right;"><link displaytype="image" src="__Jump2Top.png" type="topiclink" href=""><title translate="true">Jump to top of page</title></link></para>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table></para>
    <list id="2" type="ul" listtype="bullet" formatstring="&#167;" format-charset="SYMBOL_CHARSET" levelreset="true" legalstyle="false" startfrom="1" styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px; font-family:Wingdings; font-size:10pt; color:#000000;">
      <li styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">This is your central work area for managing search paths. It shows all defined search paths for the selected compiler target in the target list. </text></li>
      <li styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">The list is actually no list but an editable TMemo; this allows you to quickly delete multiple lines or transfer paths and individual folder names using copy and paste. </text></li>
      <li styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">It is possible to drop directories from the Windows Explorer on the memo to add them. </text></li>
    </list>
    <list id="4" type="ul" listtype="bullet" formatstring="&#167;" format-charset="SYMBOL_CHARSET" levelreset="true" legalstyle="false" startfrom="1" styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px; font-family:Wingdings; font-size:10pt; color:#000000;">
      <li styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">The alternative way to add directories is to use the </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-style:italic; color:#800000;" translate="true">&quot;Fav&quot;</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true"> (favorites) button. The button shows a pop up from which you can select a favorite or open the favorites configuration dialog. If no favorites have been configured, the button immediately shows the favorites configuration dialog. A single favorite entry can contain multiple directories, so it is e.g. possible to add all directories necessary for libraries like Indy, JCL or JVCL with one click rather than having to add each of them separately. </text></li>
    </list>
    <list id="5" type="ul" listtype="bullet" formatstring="&#167;" format-charset="SYMBOL_CHARSET" levelreset="true" legalstyle="false" startfrom="1" styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px; font-family:Wingdings; font-size:10pt; color:#000000;">
      <li styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">With the </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-style:italic; color:#800000;" translate="true">up / down buttons</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true"> or with </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-style:italic; color:#800000;" translate="true">Ctrl + up/down arrow keys</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true"> you can change the order of the directory entries and thus their search priority and the compiler speed. </text></li>
    </list>
    <list id="6" type="ul" listtype="bullet" formatstring="&#167;" format-charset="SYMBOL_CHARSET" levelreset="true" legalstyle="false" startfrom="1" styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px; font-family:Wingdings; font-size:10pt; color:#000000;">
      <li styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">Using the buttons </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-style:italic;" translate="true">&quot;</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-style:italic; color:#800000;" translate="true">Make Relative</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-style:italic;" translate="true">&quot;</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true"> or </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-style:italic;" translate="true">&quot;</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-style:italic; color:#800000;" translate="true">Make Absolute</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-style:italic;" translate="true">&quot;</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true"> all directories in the memo will be made relative to the project file directory or absolute respectively. </text></li>
    </list>
    <list id="7" type="ul" listtype="bullet" formatstring="&#167;" format-charset="SYMBOL_CHARSET" levelreset="true" legalstyle="false" startfrom="1" styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px; font-family:Wingdings; font-size:10pt; color:#000000;">
      <li styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">With the buttons </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-style:italic; color:#800000;" translate="true">&quot;Prepend ..\&quot;</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true"> or </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; font-style:italic; color:#800000;" translate="true">&quot;Remove ..\&quot;</text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true"> you can add or remove a relative path prefix for the currently selected line(s) to specify a parent or child directory as the starting point for the path specification. </text></li>
    </list>
    <para styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:6px; margin-right:6px; margin-left:6px;"><table styleclass="Default" rowcount="2" colcount="2" style="width:100%; background-color:#f4f4f4;">
      <tr style="vertical-align:top">
        <td style="width:48px;">
          <para styleclass="Normal" style="margin-top:3px; margin-bottom:3px; margin-left:6px;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana; color:#ff0000;" translate="true">Notice</text></para>
        </td>
        <td style="vertical-align:top;">
          <list id="8" type="ul" listtype="bullet" formatstring="&#167;" format-charset="SYMBOL_CHARSET" levelreset="true" legalstyle="false" startfrom="1" styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:3px; margin-right:6px; margin-bottom:3px; margin-left:8px; font-family:Wingdings; font-size:10pt; color:#000000;">
            <li styleclass="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-top:3px; margin-right:6px; margin-bottom:3px; margin-left:8px;"><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-family:Verdana;" translate="true">The ability to edit data without restrictions requires disciplined work, as the accessibility of the paths is not checked by the application. This option is very powerful, but you should know exactly what you are doing and whether your path specification references a correct directory under all circumstances. </text></li>
          </list>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr style="vertical-align:top">
        <td style="width:48px;">
